{
  "_notes": [
    "This is the exact demo/sample data from prototype.html, cleaned up for use as seed data in the production build.",
    "Dates in the prototype are generated relative to 'today' (WEEK_DATES[0..6] = Mon..Sun of the current week, with some entries on 'last week' to demo mid-week rate changes). For seeding a real dev/test environment, treat 'day' below as an offset from whatever week you're seeding (0=Monday) and 'week' as 'current' or 'previous'.",
    "Rate history is modeled as an append-only list of {rate, from} per worker and per client (and optionally per client+service-type), never an overwritten single number — this is a core data-model invariant from the spec, not just a demo quirk.",
    "Two rows are deliberately seeded with a *second*, later-dated rate so Payroll/Billing have a real example of a week that splits across an old and new rate: Maria Silva's pay rate, and Locale's billing rate."
  ],

